WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
I like to start speaking when I have
about 3,000 known words in a language.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:10.769
This is what I'm finding right now. Some
people may start to speak earlier, some

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:15.299
people may want to delay it. It depends
on your personality, it depends on the

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:18.660
language you're learning, how different
it is from languages that you already

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.090
know, how much common vocabulary there is
and so forth. But eventually you should

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:29.429
speak. You should schedule with one of
our tutors, or if we don't have a tutor

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:34.620
in that language, you can use one of the
other communities online such as italki,

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:40.260
which offers native speaker
tutors. Whether you're with a LingQ tutor

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.600
or someone at italki, make sure you get
a report with the words and phrases, at

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.559
least some of them, the words and phrases
that you had difficulty with so that

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:55.100
this report can be imported into LingQ
and that you can study it and hopefully

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:01.829
eventually improve. But it takes a long
time to get to a level of fluency, so

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:08.180
make sure you're patient but do force
yourself at some point to start speaking.

